<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <RootNamespace>$(MSBuildProjectName)</RootNamespace>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <!-- the packages carry XML documentation. The missing-comment warning is off here, and back on
         for the libraries, whose public API is documented in full. (The SDK derives the
         documentation file name before Directory.Build.targets is read, so this lives here.) -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Product>Distaff</Product>
    <Authors>Jeff Nyman</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) Jeff Nyman. Portions derived from ScummVM, copyright the ScummVM Team; from Munt, copyright its authors; and from Daventry and Maniacal, copyright Jeff Nyman.</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>GPL-3.0-or-later</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/jeffnyman/distaff</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/jeffnyman/distaff</PackageProjectUrl>
    <!-- dotnet pack -p:VersionSuffix=alpha.2 for the next prerelease; an empty suffix is a release -->
    <VersionPrefix>0.2.0</VersionPrefix>
    <VersionSuffix>alpha</VersionSuffix>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageTags>scumm;loom;lucasfilm;adventure;interpreter;scummvm;retro;games;fm-towns;mt-32</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Second prerelease: the libraries' public API, chosen and documented, on the way to 1.0. Breaking for code written against 0.1.0-alpha, whose libraries made nearly all of the engine public. New: Loom, the front door (Loom.Open, then Play, Inspect or CreateEngine); GameInspector, for a room's picture and objects and a script disassembled; GameWorld's snapshots (GetActor, ActorsHere, RunningScripts, ShownVerbs) in place of the engine's own objects, with Audio, MusicVolume, SfxVolume, CameraX and Variables. Now internal: the engine's rooms, costumes, scripts, sound players, screens and resources, and in Distaff.Audio the FLAC and Vorbis decoders and Munt's settings. Every public member is documented, and the surface is kept in PublicAPI.*.txt. Fixed: the VGA CD's message dialogs (printString in slot 3) show, as ScummVM's original interface shows them: the opening ends on "Press F9 to toggle text on screen ON/OFF", waiting for a key, and F9 says whether the text appears. A script the inspector cannot decode gives its ScriptListing an Error. New in the player: --version.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' == 'true'">
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
